// Change: new rule
// Title: Binary Executed From A Temporal Directory By Node
// Sigma ID: f01212bd-5f6c-4d99-acad-d088456e8fee
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: thereisnobackup
// Date: 2026-07-18 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: initial-access, T1195.001, execution, T1059.007, stealth, T1027.009
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Generic pattern inspired by the jscrambler npm supply chain compromise: detects a .exe launched
//   from a temp directory by a node-related parent process.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://socket.dev/blog/jscrambler-supply-chain-attack
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/165afff3c8086783fe27ef794bc7e8635366f621/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_temp_dir_binary_exec_by_node.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\node" and ProcessCommandLine endswith ".exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Windows\\Temp\\")
